<title>USA: Stanford Telecom gets two contracts.</title>
<headline>Stanford Telecom gets two contracts.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stanford Telecommunications Inc said Tuesday it had been awarded two Defense Satellite Communications System (DSCS) contracts with an aggregate value of $58 million.</p>
<p>Thee contract awards continue Stanford Telecom's 15-year role in the evolutionary development and support of the DSCS Operations Control System (DOCS).</p>
<p>The contracts were awarded during the company's fiscal third quarter, ended December 31. During the quarter, the company will recognize initial funded bookings totaling $5 million against these contracts.</p>
</text>
